WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

7
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

8
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

9
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

10
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

11
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

12
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

13
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

14
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

15
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

16
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

17
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

18
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

19
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

20
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

21
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

22
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

23
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

24
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

25
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

26
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

27
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

28
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.220
<b>Spin, Pinwheel, Spin</b>

29
00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.240
– Big Bro won!
– Big Bro won!

30
00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.430
Arlong Park has fallen!

31
00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.690
Nojiko... Is all of this really happening...?

32
00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.610
Surely this is a dream.

33
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.540
Luffy! Luffy! Luffy!

34
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.790
Luffy?

35
00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:25.420
Luffy! Luffy! Luffy! Luffy? Good job, Luffy!
You almost did as good as me. Let's face it, I'm

36
00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.500
pretty much the star,
but I'll cheer for you anyway

37
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.090
because I'm super modest,
and I don't want to steal your thunder.

38
00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.050
You really had us going there, Luffy.

39
00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:39.510
Start dealin' with the bad guys quicker.
I almost had a heart attack... You rubber jerk!

40
00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:41.320
Luffy?

41
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.500
Luffy! Luffy! Luffy!

42
00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:50.380
Luffy! Luffy!

43
00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.090
This is awesome!

44
00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.800
Okay! Hold it right there!

45
00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.100
Damn! It's him!

46
00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.860
What a lucky day today is.

47
00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:34.740
Very nice. I saw the entire fight
and I must say, good work!

48
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:39.280
I can only assume that your victory
here was some sort of bizarre accident.

49
00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.080
I never thought that the fishmen would lose
to riff-raff like you and your crew.

50
00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.620
However, now that Arlong is out
of the picture, I'll be taking all

51
00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.960
the money I was supposed to give to him
in addition to all the treasure in Arlong Park.

52
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.300
Now drop your weapons!

53
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.510
Colonel Nezumi of Branch Sixteen

54
00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.430
gets all the credit!

55
00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.100
Zoro!

56
00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:04.850
I see you're trying to rain on these people's
parade... Now that's just plain rude.

57
00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:15.150
Go on, you scum, just try it.
You'll be sorry, I promise you that.

58
00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.570
He's still at it.

59
00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.700
This is for shooting Nojiko.

60
00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.620
And also for mercilessly destroying
Bellemere's tangerine orchard.

61
00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.210
Colonel!

62
00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.590
Thanks, Nami. That felt good.

63
00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.090
A thousand more
and we'll call it even!

64
00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:51.650
What you're gonna do is clean up
after those fishmen.

65
00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.020
Then you're gonna help
to rebuild the town of Gosa,

66
00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.110
and you won't lay a finger
on any of the money or valuables in Arlong Park.

67
00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.490
That's the island's money
now! Got it?!

68
00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:04.410
Right! Yeah! I'll do anything you say!

69
00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:05.990
And there's one more thing!

70
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.200
Give me my money back, jerk!

71
00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:13.670
I promise! I promise!
I'll give every berry back!

72
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.510
I'll get you, you pirates!

73
00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.090
Luffy is your Captain, right?

74
00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:25.100
Well, mark my freaking words, rubber man,

75
00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.060
major things are gonna happen
'cause you made me angry!

76
00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.430
I swear you'll regret this!

77
00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.190
I'll get my revenge!
Just you wait and see!

78
00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.690
Major things are gonna happen?

79
00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.070
And I'm gonna be King of the Pirates.

80
00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:42.950
That's not what he means at all.
Are you really that clueless?!

81
00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:46.530
Hold on! What next?!
Are we in super big trouble, or what?!

82
00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.580
Hey! Hey! What do we do?!

83
00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.080
Now's not the time
to keep this to ourselves!

84
00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.340
We need to tell everyone on the island
what happened here today!

85
00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.840
Arlong Park has fallen!

86
00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.150
Hey, Zoro! What's
that on your chest?

87
00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.060
[GENZO]
Huh?

88
00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.860
What are you...

89
00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.400
Good job, Nami.

90
00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:24.740
Our island would be saved
by unruly pirates.

91
00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.740
The world is strange.

92
00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.550
[NOJIKO]
Why are you
still here, Nami?

93
00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.560
[NOJIKO]
Your friends
have been looking for you.

94
00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.180
[NAMI]
Hey, Nojiko.

95
00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:53.680
Huh?

96
00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.520
Genzo...

97
00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.650
If Bell-mère were still alive

98
00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.610
and I wanted to become a pirate
do you think she'd let me do it?

99
00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.610
A pirate...?

100
00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.990
What do you think?
Of course she'd never let her

101
00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:08.240
precious daughter go out to sea
with a bunch of treacherous pirates.

102
00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:09.910
Yeah, she'd let you!

103
00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:09.910
Nojiko!

104
00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.770
But if she had said 'no,'

105
00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.540
that wouldn't stop you, would it?

106
00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.540
That's right. Nope.

107
00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:21.500
[GENZO]
I see...

108
00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.190
What's up, Genzo?

109
00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.970
You certainly are
Bellemere's kids. Ha, ha.

110
00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.270
Oh, yeah?

111
00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.770
Nami, you've already made up
your mind about this.

112
00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.760
[GENZO]
There's no use
fighting it. Live your life.

113
00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:48.610
He's still at it.

114
00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:53.230
[SANJI]
Well, you saw the way
he looked after that fight.

115
00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:56.870
[USOPP]
Yeah, anyone
else would've been dead.

116
00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.960
You dumbass!

117
00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.920
Did you think this
would heal on its own?

118
00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.130
Seriously, pirates are supposed
be smarter than this.

119
00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.470
[DOCTOR]
Don't you have
a ship's doctor?

120
00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:12.890
[LUFFY]
Doctor? Never thought
of that. Good idea.

121
00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:13.760
Luffy?

122
00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.140
But we need to get
a musician first, right?

123
00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.390
Why's that?

124
00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.650
Because pirates really like to sing.

125
00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:22.310
That's true, but why's that first?

126
00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.320
Hello? Hello?

127
00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:27.820
<b>Marine Base (16th Branch)</b>

128
00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:26.190
Yes. This is Navy Headquarters.

129
00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.950
Headquarters! Right! Good!

130
00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:32.490
Hello! Hello. This is Colonel Nezumi
of Marine Branch Sixteen, Marine Code

131
00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.080
00733.

132
00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.250
<b>Transponder Snail
16th Marine Branch</b>

133
00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:36.950
I have a request!

134
00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.330
There really is no reason
to shout. I can hear you.

135
00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:47.470
Listen! There's a pirate who wears
a straw hat. He's named Luffy.

136
00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:47.470
<b>Transponder Snail
Marine HQ</b>

137
00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:57.060
I hereby declare that he and his four
crewmembers are enemies of the government!

138
00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:56.390
<b>Marine HQ Information Office</b>

139
00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.560
Luffy... Alright

140
00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.100
They managed to take down

141
00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.940
the purportedly invincible
Fish-Man Arlong at his home base.

142
00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.570
Based on the grave threat
they present, a large bounty

143
00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:10.070
has been placed
on their captain, Straw Hat Luffy.

144
00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.700
Transmitting photograph now.

145
00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.780
Roger that.

146
00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:17.500
Huh?

147
00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:20.250
Couldn't you have taken
a better picture than that.

148
00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.000
No... Sorry sir.

149
00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:26.960
Okay. Right after a quick verification,
I'll send it in for approval, sir.

150
00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:32.300
Don't forget, he's
a wanted pirate! Dead or alive!

151
00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:37.180
I want his face on posters
all over the world!

152
00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:51.700
[SANJI]
Boy am I stuffed.

153
00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.070
It's nice to not have
to cook for a change.

154
00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.950
So, how're you feelin', Zoro?

155
00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.950
I'll be okay. I think
all I need's a little bit a rest.

156
00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.370
That's good.

157
00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.750
[ZORO]
Seriously, how much
longer can they keep this up?

158
00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.710
It's been three days now.

159
00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.050
Nothing wrong with that.

160
00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:11.670
Smoke 'em if ya got 'em.

161
00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.510
[LUFFY]
Hey, Sanji...
Where'd you get that melon you had.

162
00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.890
I want to give it a try.

163
00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:19.270
It isn't polite to talk
with your mouth full.

164
00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.730
[SANJI]
I dunno. It was a raw ham melon
with raw ham on top.

165
00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.810
[LUFFY]
Raw ham melon?!
Show me where you found it!

166
00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:26.360
[SANJI]
I can't.

167
00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:31.690
The whole town is basically
one giant buffet. Good luck finding it.

168
00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.700
He ran off.

169
00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.030
Three days of stuffing his face.

170
00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.030
And now that my belly's full.

171
00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:40.910
Time to dance!

172
00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:46.580
[USOPP]
I am Captain Usopp!

173
00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.340
Can I have your autograph?

174
00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:50.130
I destroyed the strongest
of all the fishmen!

175
00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.930
Let's sing about me, let's sing!

176
00:10:54.930 --> 00:11:00.680
♪ I am the greatest,
my friends. ♪

177
00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:01.060
I'm so bored.

178
00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:01.680
[CHABO]
Hm?

179
00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.230
I thought you'd be more upset.

180
00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:08.110
Why didn't this happen before my daddy died?
Why is life so unfair?

181
00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.480
That.

182
00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.070
I was kinda upset, at first...

183
00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:15.990
But I decided just
to think about my future.

184
00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.570
What about it?

185
00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:21.370
[CHABO]
We were saved
by the straw hat guy and his friends.

186
00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:26.210
But tomorrow we have to start all over again,
on our own, without anybody's help.

187
00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:31.420
We can't forget the past...
but... now... it's

188
00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:35.510
really up to us what happens. There's no one
to blame our problems on anymore.

189
00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:38.590
We can succeed or fail.
It all depends on our choices.

190
00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.470
Whining about the past
gets us nowhere.

191
00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.770
I decided to think that way.

192
00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:47.600
That so?

193
00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.850
Stop, ow, ow, let

194
00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.860
go, stop that hurts, ow, stop ow!

195
00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:54.110
It's no fun if I can't harass
you for being a baby.

196
00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:58.110
So you decided to hurt me instead?!
You stupid old punk!

197
00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:05.410
Punk... That's right!

198
00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:09.830
[NAMI]
Can you get rid of it?

199
00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.500
[DOCTOR]
I'll do my best. But you do

200
00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.010
realize this is a tattoo.

201
00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:20.970
[NAMI]
Heh. I was stupid.
I knew it wouldn't come off.

202
00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:23.760
[NAMI cries]
I don't want
anyone to see this!

203
00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.560
This... This awful tattoo.

204
00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:32.500
I'm just pretending but it's
like he owns me now.

205
00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.240
Nami.

206
00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.200
[NAMI]
Nojiko, what is that?

207
00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.080
[NOJIKO]
Oh, you mean this?

208
00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.040
It's nothing, just a tattoo.

209
00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.970
Now I look just like you.

210
00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.260
[NAMI]
Hey, Doc.

211
00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:00.340
[NAMI]
I think I'd like a new tattoo.

212
00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:02.720
[NAMI]
Like this.

213
00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:05.260
Look at those

214
00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:10.130
Let's stand as we sing.

215
00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.900
[GENZO]
Bell-mère.

216
00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:20.150
Your daughters are strong young women
now. You'd be so proud.

217
00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:24.330
It's like I'm standing right
in front of you again.

218
00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:29.290
[GENZO]
We're not going to waste
a single moment now. So much has been lost.

219
00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:32.790
Everyone has had to make
terrible sacrifices. Which is why

220
00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:38.090
I don't care if I look like a fool, I'm happy
for the first time in a long while.

221
00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.590
[LUFFY]
Raw ham melon!

222
00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:46.600
no food up here.

223
00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:47.560
Guess I'll go back Be quiet!

224
00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:51.850
[LUFFY]
A grave? Did somebody die?

225
00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.060
[GENZO]
Yes. A long time ago.

226
00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:59.030
Oh, I'm sorry. I give you
to my conveniences.

227
00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:04.160
Wait, my sincere compliments.
Nope... My darkest concussion?

228
00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.410
[GENZO]
My deepest condolences.

229
00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.120
[LUFFY]
Thanks!

230
00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.410
[GENZO]
Listen, boy.

231
00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.960
I know Nami's going away with you.
She has her mind set on becoming a pirate,

232
00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.960
and that's dangerous business.

233
00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:18.090
And I'm fine with that.

234
00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:20.760
It can't be helped.

235
00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:24.260
But if any of you ever do
anything to hurt her,

236
00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.720
I will kill you.

237
00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.680
[LUFFY]
We're not going to hurt her.

238
00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.140
You sure?!

239
00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.100
I'm sure.

240
00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:02.130
<b>I'm leaving</b>
<b>this</b>
<b>behind.</b>
<b>It</b>
<b>belongs</b>
<b>to</b>
<b>village.</b>
<b>the</b>
<b>Nami</b>

241
00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:11.310
[NAMI]
Wow, what's up
with all the food?

242
00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:14.040
[BELL-MÈRE]
Do you two know
what today is?

243
00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:14.560
[NAMI, NOJIKO]
– Huh?
– Huh?

244
00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:18.690
It's the anniversary...
...of the day we met!

245
00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:22.630
We're celebrating the day
you became my daughters.

246
00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.410
Hey, don't cry.

247
00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:31.540
It's just a storm.
So what if it ruins our crops?

248
00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:36.000
You need to learn to be strong girls
who can smile even during hard times.

249
00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:40.250
Do that, and nothing
will ever stop you.

250
00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.920
[BELL-MÈRE]
Now
show me those smiles.

251
00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.440
Nami, will you go get the salt?

252
00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.220
I see you can draw land maps
now as well as sea charts.

253
00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:54.270
I wanted the book
to study navigation.

254
00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.390
Navigation as well?

255
00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:59.060
– You're gonna be a navigator?
– That's right,

256
00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:02.940
I'm gonna guide ships around all the oceans
of the world. It'll be great.

257
00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.570
And I'll be able to make
maps of all the far off places I'll go.

258
00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:11.490
So, this island map is a first step
toward realizing your dream, is that it?

259
00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:13.040
Yeah!

260
00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.740
[NAMI]
Well, Bell-mère.
We finally made it...

261
00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.820
It took eight long years
but we're finally free.

262
00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.490
The village... and me.

263
00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:55.950
It's just like you told us
when we were children.

264
00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.830
"Be brave and smile,
and nothing will be able to stop you."

265
00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.210
It's so true.

266
00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.840
Arlong's gone. And now everybody
is so happy to be free.

267
00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:10.180
And me? I'm finally gonna
leave this island.

268
00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.930
But don't worry. I'll be okay.

269
00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:17.640
I'm going with good, strong people like you.

270
00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:23.270
And this last map is all that
I have left to remind me,

271
00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.610
but none of that really
matters anymore, right?

272
00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:32.200
Cause now. I'll start again... And every map
I draw will be for me and nobody else.

273
00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:36.410
Oh, you see. This time when I see the world
it will be with all of my friends.

274
00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.330
You know that's
what I've always wanted.

275
00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:42.830
Anyway.

276
00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:47.590
I'm just trying to say goodbye
cause I don't know if I'll be back.

277
00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:59.280
[NAMI]
I'm going now, okay?

278
00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:22.000
<b>The Morning of Departure</b>

279
00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.770
[USOPP]
This is the last one, right?

280
00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:27.380
[ZORO]
Yeah.

281
00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:28.630
[LUFFY]
We got everything?

282
00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:29.500
[USOPP]
Yup!

283
00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.380
Alright. We're stocked up
with everything we need.

284
00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.290
I think we're good to go.

285
00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:36.760
[USOPP grunts]
You know
we've only been on this little island

286
00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:39.100
for a few days but it feels
more like a lifetime.

287
00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.520
[laughs]
Yeah!

288
00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:51.070
[SANJI]
Hm? We can't thank you enough
for everything you've done for us,

289
00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:54.490
but we gotta go back
to our regular jobs as bounty hunters.

290
00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:55.410
So, this is goodbye.

291
00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.910
I hope we get
to meet again someday.

292
00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:00.870
See ya 'round.

293
00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.120
[JOHNNY, YOSAKU]
– Goodbye!
– Goodbye!

294
00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.330
Yeah, now it's time
for us to get going.

295
00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.570
But we can't leave
yet– we gotta wait for Nami.

296
00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.050
Well, maybe she's not coming.

297
00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:13.090
Uhh. What, why not?!

298
00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:17.090
If you try to hit on her again,
I swear I'll break your freakin' neck! You got it?!

299
00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.350
Why would I do something like that?

300
00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:20.100
[USOPP]
She might
not even be coming.

301
00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:24.230
After all, she has achieved her goal.
Nami doesn't have to be a pirate anymore.

302
00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.230
She might be better off if she stayed

303
00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:27.600
here on this island

304
00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:27.780
with all her friends and family.

305
00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:29.060
What about me, dammit?!

306
00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:32.730
Without Nami onboard
I have like 98.72% less reason

307
00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:36.070
to stay with you people
on this stupid pirate ship.

308
00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:39.070
Hey, I'm still upset with you
about the raw ham melon!

309
00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:40.700
Why isn't Nami here?

310
00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.620
Don't know. I haven't seen
her anywhere since this morning.

311
00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:44.250
[GENZO]
What?!

312
00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.540
One-hundred million berries?

313
00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.750
She left all of the money?

314
00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.040
She's not even gonna
take some of it?

315
00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:53.840
But she worked so hard to get it.

316
00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:57.010
She'll steal more.
That's what her letter said.

317
00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:01.010
There's no changing her mind
once it's made up.

318
00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:02.760
That girl.

319
00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.480
She didn't even give us a chance
to thank her. Hm?

320
00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:07.280
[LUFFY gasps]

321
00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:08.210
[USOPP, ZORO gasp]

322
00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:09.370
[SANJI screams]

323
00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.900
[SANJI]
There she is!

324
00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.280
[GENZO]
Nami!

325
00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.280
[NOJIKO]
Nami!

326
00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:16.400
[VILLAGERS]
– Nami!
– Nami!

327
00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:17.740
Set the sails!

328
00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:26.660
I don't get it. Why's she running?

329
00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:27.910
[LUFFY]
She said to set sail.

330
00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:28.500
What?

331
00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.460
No, she's planning

332
00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:35.300
on leaving us without letting
any of us thank her or say goodbye.

333
00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:36.210
Hey, wait!

334
00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.880
[LUFFY]
Set sail

335
00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.260
[VILLAGER A]
Wait!

336
00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:45.930
Don't go!

337
00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:46.460
[VILLAGER B]
They're leaving!

338
00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.690
[DOCTOR]
Stop!
At least let us say goodbye!

339
00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:51.650
[VILLAGER A]
Nami, don't!

340
00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.110
[VILLAGER B]
Let us thank you!

341
00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:58.860
Nami! Come back here
you can't leave this way!

342
00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:02.120
So, you sure you want
to let her leave like this?

343
00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.830
Not my decision.
She does what she wants.

344
00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:23.600
Nami!

345
00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.070
Why?!

346
00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:56.960
Huh?! No way!

347
00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:58.380
[VILLAGER A]
Hey,
where's my money?!

348
00:21:58.380 --> 00:21:59.710
[VILLAGER B]
My wallet's gone!

349
00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:01.050
[VILLAGER C]
Mine, too!

350
00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:03.680
[VILLAGER D]
– She stole my money!
– My purse is gone!

351
00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:08.890
Thanks a bunch!

352
00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:13.980
– Damn! You little brat!
– Damn! You little brat!

353
00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:17.940
Great, she hasn't changed a bit.

354
00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.780
I'd watch my back.

355
00:22:19.790 --> 00:22:24.160
[LUFFY, SANJI laughing]

356
00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.780
[GENZO]
You lousy pickpocket!

357
00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:27.660
We'll miss you!

358
00:22:35.210 --> 00:22:36.590
[GENZO]
Boy!

359
00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:40.420
Remember what I told you.

360
00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:44.550
[LUFFY]
You got it!

361
00:22:44.470 --> 00:22:47.550
[NAMI]
Goodbye everybody!
I'll miss you. Take care.

362
00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:52.560
[NOJIKO laughing]
I can't believe her!

363
00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:55.350
My little sister got us good
with that one.

364
00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:58.060
Be safe, Nami.

365
00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:04.320
[DOCTOR]
Take a look at this.

366
00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:06.620
[GENZO]
What is it Doc... Nami's bill?

367
00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:12.620
[DOCTOR]
Not exactly. That girl
will never change. That's her new tattoo.

368
00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:14.750
[GENZO]
– What's it supposed
to be? – A tangerine

369
00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:17.750
and a pinwheel.

370
00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:22.420
Hey, Genzo. Where's your pinwheel?

371
00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:28.550
[GENZO laughs]
I
don't need it anymore.

372
00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:41.570
[NAMI]
I'm off.

373
00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:45.310
Ah, man.

374
00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:51.870
[BELL-MÈRE]
Genzo, back off.
Don't get so close to Nami.

375
00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:55.500
[GENZO]
I just wanted
to see her smile.

376
00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:58.710
[BELL-MÈRE]
Your face is too scary.
It's making her cry.

377
00:23:58.710 --> 00:24:01.210
[GENZO]
I can't change my face...

378
00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:02.380
Oh, wait...

379
00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:06.300
I'll keep this on my hat
to distract her.

380
00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:08.340
What do ya think little girl?

381
00:24:08.340 --> 00:24:09.840
[BELL-MÈRE]
You're joking, right?

382
00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:13.370
It's just a stupid pinwheel. There's
no way it's going to make her–

383
00:24:13.370 --> 00:24:16.560
[laughing]

384
00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:22.700
[BELL-MÈRE]
I can't believe
it. She's laughing.

385
00:24:39.390 --> 00:24:44.380
More feelings than I can hold but I can’t make you understand

386
00:24:44.400 --> 00:24:49.240
Be that as it may, I just can’t bear to let go of your hand

387
00:24:49.290 --> 00:24:54.190
I’ve still gotta move, even if I’m alone I’ll walk along

388
00:24:54.230 --> 00:24:59.460
Just promise that you’ll still keep an eye on me when I am gone Just promise that you’ll still keep an eye on me when I am gone

389
00:25:04.110 --> 00:25:08.990
As soon as I woke up, couldn’t get it off my mind

390
00:25:09.040 --> 00:25:13.740
“Why the hell’s it so hot? I can hardly breathe!”

391
00:25:13.740 --> 00:25:20.250
It’s been quite a while, but those thoughts just won’t seem to let go It’s been quite a while, but those thoughts just won’t seem to let go

392
00:25:20.250 --> 00:25:24.130
But hey, what do I know?

393
00:25:25.080 --> 00:25:30.000
Guess I want a taste of that thing people call a “runner’s high”

394
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:34.870
Think I chased too hard, and ended up leaving myself behind

395
00:25:34.920 --> 00:25:39.860
All I want’s a taste of a dream that a sentence can’t define

396
00:25:39.860 --> 00:25:45.050
Stick right by my side, and I can run, run, run until I die
